    {
      "id": 296182,
      "name": "Cyclade Island Architecture",
      "note": "<p>One of the most well-known types of Greek architecture; houses with</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>completely white walls</strong></li>\n<li><strong>blue doors</strong></li>\n<li><strong>and shutters</strong>\nIs mainly found on the small central <strong>Cyclade islands</strong>.</li>\n</ul>",
      "images": [
        "https://learnablemeta.com/images/1278/mV7X3tYlXD3rPKIOhTjAfAhDPYgg5IRkMjQu.avif"
      ],
      "locationsCount": 8,
      "footer": "Description and images taken from:  <a href=\"https://www.plonkit.net/greece\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">www.plonkit.net/greece</a>."
    },
    {
      "id": 334293,
      "name": "Epirotic Architecture",
      "note": "<p><strong>Grey stone houses</strong> with <strong>slate roofs</strong> are typical for <strong>Epiru</strong>s, especially around <strong>Vikos Gorge</strong> in <strong>Pindus National Park</strong>. Even single grey stone houses are a good hint for this region.</p>",
      "images": [
        "https://learnablemeta.com/images/1279/5ZednNtUhpSDmpMy2UCCcBjec52u33G5pHay.avif"
      ],
      "locationsCount": 6,
      "footer": "<p><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1zmdDA3a4tkoAzshgASNzvThVyXFGAC9Rnpcjn_vUr34/edit?usp=sharing\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Greece doc</a></p>"
    },
    {
      "id": 296193,
      "name": "Fir Trees",
      "note": "<p>Unlike the Northern Pindus, in the Southern half of the <strong>Pindus range</strong>, <strong>fir</strong> trees are the <strong>dominant species</strong>.</p>",
      "images": [
        "https://learnablemeta.com/images/1278/CnxzPJxGy1XKOkgHaY05oyUhOUqhX3t0H9sQ.avif"
      ],
      "locationsCount": 6,
